# Project One Get-Item Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: get-item and inventory design for M7 Project Two
#
# Review the course-provided get-item flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, SET, ADD, or similar terms.

START get_item

    # Identify the current room, item, and inventory.
    SET current_room
    SET item_in_room
    SET inventory

    # Prompt the player for the item they want to collect.

    OUTPUT "Enter the item you want to get:"
    INPUT requested_item


   # Check whether the requested item is in the current room.
    IF requested_item IS item_in_room THEN


    # Add the item to the player's inventory.
    ADD requested_item TO inventory

    # Remove the item from the current room.
    SET item_in_room TO NONE

    # Tell the player the item was collected.
    OUTPUT "You picked up the " + requested_item + "."

ELSE

    # The requested item is not available in the current room.
    OUTPUT "That item is not in this room."

END IF


    # Return to the main gameplay loop so the player can enter another command.
OUTPUT "Enter your next command."
RETURN TO GAME LOOP

END get_item


